---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const updated = "October 23, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Escape From WP"
  description="How Escape From WP handles the information you give us: your email, the URL you submit, basic anti-abuse data, and the third-party services involved."
>
  <header class="nav">
    <div class="wrap nav-inner">
      <a href={`${base}/`} class="wordmark">ESCAPE&nbsp;FROM&nbsp;<span class="wp">WP</span></a>
      <a href={`${base}/liberate/`} class="nav-link">Liberate a site →</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="legal-wrap">
    <section class="legal">
      <span class="eyebrow">◦ Legal · Privacy</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>
        Escape From WP (<strong>escapefromwp.com</strong>) is a free tool that copies a public
        website you submit and rebuilds it as a self-contained EmDash or static site. This policy
        explains what we collect, why, and who else is involved. We keep it short because we keep
        the data minimal.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your email address.</strong> You give it to us so we can email you the download
          link when your rebuilt site is ready. If you opt in, we also use it to follow up about
          moving off WordPress. You can ask us to delete it at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The website URL you submit.</strong> We fetch that public site, render its pages,
          and download its images and fonts to build your copy. We only process sites you confirm
          you own or have the right to copy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Basic anti-abuse data.</strong> To stop spam and abuse we record a one-way hashed
          form of your IP address (not the raw IP) and rate-limit how many builds come from the same
          source. We do not use this to track you across other websites.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies &amp; analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics to understand, in aggregate, how the site is used (page views,
        rough traffic sources). This sets analytics cookies. We do not sell your data or run
        advertising trackers.
      </p>

      <h2>Bot protection — Cloudflare Turnstile</h2>
      <p>
        To tell real visitors from bots, our forms are protected by
        <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile</strong>. Turnstile runs silently in the background and may
        collect information about your device and browser to make that determination. Cloudflare
        processes this on our behalf. Your use of Turnstile on this site is governed by Cloudflare's
        <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/turnstile-privacy-policy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Turnstile Privacy Addendum</a>
        and Cloudflare's
        <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Other services we rely on</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, storage, and the build pipeline for your copied site.</li>
        <li><strong>WordPress.com / rendering infrastructure</strong> — used to capture and render the public site you submit.</li>
        <li><strong>Our email provider</strong> — used only to send you the download link and any follow-up you opted into.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep things</h2>
      <p>
        Download links and the rebuilt copy are temporary and expire. We don't keep an archive of
        copied sites. Your email stays on file only as long as needed to deliver your download and,
        if you opted in, to follow up — until you ask us to remove it.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Want your email removed, or have a question about your data? Email us at
        <a href="mailto:james@apexbranding.design">james@apexbranding.design</a> and we'll take care of it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, we'll update the date at the top of this page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="wrap footer-inner">
      <span class="wordmark small">ESCAPE&nbsp;FROM&nbsp;<span class="wp">WP</span></span>
      <span class="footer-mono">◦ WordPress migration &amp; rescue · escapefromwp.com</span>
      <span class="footer-mono dim">© {new Date().getFullYear()} — All units accounted for.</span>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-wrap { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 120px 20px 80px; }
  .legal .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .14em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--signal-red); display: block; margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .legal h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 48px); line-height: 1.05; margin: 0 0 8px; color: var(--chalk); }
  .legal-updated { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--steel-2, #8a8f98); margin: 0 0 32px; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 20px; margin: 36px 0 10px; color: var(--chalk); }
  .legal p, .legal li { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ash, #c7ccd1); }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 20px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .legal a { color: var(--signal-red); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .legal a:hover { opacity: .85; }
  .nav-link { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--chalk); text-decoration: none; }
</style>
